    {
      "id": "bulletproof-react",
      "repository": "https://github.com/alan2207/bulletproof-react",
      "revision": "9506629ed003a561c6627735480cce4994244bb4",
      "description": "bulletproof-react Vite app (createBrowserRouter data router, MSW mocks)",
      "framework": "react-router",
      "workingDirectory": "apps/react-vite",
      "install": "cd apps/react-vite && yarn install && cp -n .env.example .env; true",
      "dev": "yarn dev",
      "url": "http://localhost:3000/",
      "settleMs": 6000,
      "static": {
        "rootDirectory": "apps/react-vite",
        "entry": "src/main.tsx",
        "route": "/",
        "externalPackageAllowList": [
          "react-helmet-async",
          "react-error-boundary",
          "@tanstack/react-query",
          "@tanstack/react-query-devtools",
          "lucide-react",
          "zustand",
          "react-query-auth"
        ]
      },
      "notes": "Routes are `lazy: () => import(...).then(convert)`; the static side awaits the import and materializes the module namespace through `convert`'s rest spread. QueryClientProvider, HelmetProvider, react-error-boundary and react-query-auth's AuthLoader are opaque with slotted children; Helmet's <meta> is a side effect, not a fiber, so that slot stays unmatched."
    },
    {
      "id": "cal-diy",
      "repository": "https://github.com/calcom/cal.diy",
      "revision": "abffde336e744e15cf69626c10e436d6172bc406",
      "description": "cal.diy web app login page (Next app router + pages router hybrid, Yarn 4 monorepo, Prisma over a local PostgreSQL container)",
      "framework": "next-app",
      "workingDirectory": "apps/web",
      "install": "yarn install",
      "setup": ["bash \"$BIPPY_CORPUS_SCRIPTS/cal-diy-setup.sh\""],
      "services": ["bash \"$BIPPY_CORPUS_SCRIPTS/postgres.sh\" bippy-cal-pg 5450 calendso"],
      "dev": "yarn dev",
      "url": "http://localhost:3000/auth/login",
      "readyTimeoutMs": 900000,
      "settleMs": 10000,
      "static": {
        "rootDirectory": "apps/web",
        "route": "/auth/login",
        "externalPackageAllowList": [
          "@calcom/*",
          "@coss/*",
          "@base-ui/*",
          "@floating-ui/*",
          "@radix-ui/*",
          "next-auth",
          "@tanstack/react-query",
          "@trpc/*",
          "react-inlinesvg",
          "next-themes",
          "nuqs",
          "react-hook-form",
          "framer-motion",
          "lucide-react",
          "i18next",
          "bcp-47-match",
          "accept-language-parser"
        ],
        "defines": {
          "process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_CALCOM_VERSION": "6.2.0"
        },
        "envFiles": ["../../.env"],
        "maxFiberCount": 20000
      },
      "notes": "`next.config.ts` loads the repository `.env` (written by the setup script) and sets `NEXT_PUBLIC_CALCOM_VERSION` from the root package version, which is the one define. The seeded database comes from cal.diy's own `db-seed`; `/` redirects unauthenticated visitors to the login page, which is captured directly."
    },
    {
      "id": "epic-stack",
      "repository": "https://github.com/epicweb-dev/epic-stack",
      "revision": "8473afd804b66dba6a23f317908dc35d1535e90d",
      "description": "Epic Stack (React Router framework mode, file-convention routes via react-router-auto-routes, Prisma)",
      "framework": "react-router",
      "workingDirectory": ".",
      "install": "npm install",
      "setup": [
        "test -f .env || cp .env.example .env",
        "npx prisma migrate deploy",
        "npx prisma generate --sql"
      ],
      "dev": "npm run dev",
      "url": "http://localhost:3000/",
      "readyTimeoutMs": 600000,
      "settleMs": 6000,
      "static": {
        "rootDirectory": ".",
        "entry": "app/routes.ts",
        "route": "/"
      },
      "notes": "routes.ts delegates to react-router-auto-routes; the static side mirrors its file conventions (_layout nesting, pathless _groups, $params, [.] escapes, trailing-underscore opt-outs) to rebuild the route table without running the generator. Loader data, honeypot and theme values stay unknown."
    },
